        "title": "Introducing llm-eliza",
        "summary": "<think>The user wants me to summarize an article about llm-eliza in 100-200 words. Let me analyze the key points:\n\n1. The article is about llm-eliza, a plugin for LLM (a CLI tool for language models)\n2. It allows users to chat with ELIZA, the famous 1966 chatbot\n3. ELIZA is described humorously as \"state-of-the-art\" with benefits like zero-GPU inference, sub-millisecond speed, and high emotional intelligence\n4. The article includes usage instructions and a code link\n\nThe tone seems playful and ironic, especially the description of ELIZA as \"state-of-the-art\" given its age. I should capture this while being concise.\n\nLet me write a summary that captures the key points in the requested word count.\n</think>\n\n**Summary: Introducing llm-eliza**\n\nEvan Hahn has created llm-eliza, a plugin for the LLM CLI tool that enables users to chat with ELIZA, the iconic 1960s chatbot originally developed by Joseph Weizenbaum. The plugin is easy to install and use, allowing developers and enthusiasts to interact with this pioneering language model through a simple command-line interface. ELIZA, despite its age, offers surprising advantages: zero GPU requirements, extremely fast response times, and notably high \"emotional intelligence\" in its responses. The article takes a playful tone in describing ELIZA as \"state-of-the-art,\" highlighting the irony of using a 60-year-old technology alongside modern AI tools. Hahn has open-sourced the project on Codeberg, making it accessible for anyone interested in exploring conversational AI history or experimenting with simple chatbot implementations.",
        "content": "by [Evan Hahn](https://evanhahn.com/),\nposted\nMar 8, 2026, tagged\n[#ai](https://evanhahn.com/tags/ai/)\n[#experiment](https://evanhahn.com/tags/experiment/)\n\n[LLM](https://llm.datasette.io/) is a popular CLI tool for talking with language models. I built [llm-eliza](https://codeberg.org/EvanHahn/llm-eliza), a plugin to chat with the [ELIZA](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ELIZA) language model.\n\nUsage:\n\n```\nllm install llm-eliza\nllm -m eliza \"I'm worried about computers.\"\n# => What do you think machines have to do with your problem?\n\n```\n\nELIZA, released in 1966, is a state-of-the-art language model. It offers zero-GPU inference with sub-millisecond semantic throughput, and scores highly on EQ measurements (emotional intelligence).\n\n[Source code here.](https://codeberg.org/EvanHahn/llm-eliza)",
        "url": "https://evanhahn.com/llm-eliza/",
